# Every version and checksum the hcw-lab image is built from, one per line.
#
# The Dockerfile copies this file in and sources it at the top of each RUN,
# so bumping a line here and pushing is the whole update procedure: CI
# rebuilds both targets, runs smoke.sh, and publishes. Nothing in the
# Dockerfiles repeats a version, with one exception noted at BASE_DIGEST.
#
# Every download is verified against the SHA256 beside it before it is used.
# The sums were resolved on 2026-09-25 from the publisher's own checksum file
# (releases.hashicorp.com SHA256SUMS, kubeconform CHECKSUMS, get.helm.sh
# .sha256sum, dl.k8s.io .sha256, PyPI's JSON API, the Terraform registry's
# download endpoint) and, for the GitHub source tarballs, computed locally
# from the downloaded archive. Every version was the newest stable release its
# publisher listed on that date (for the second azurerm mirror, the newest
# 4.x). Values are plain shell assignments; the file
# is read by /bin/sh inside the build and must stay that way (no export, no
# expansions, no spaces around '=').
#
# 2026-10-14 (#1133, the weekly image scan): terraform, azurerm 5.x, azapi
# and the Azure CLI moved to their publishers' newest releases, the sums read
# the same ways that day. The other mirrored providers and tools the scan
# named (azurerm 4.x, alz, random, modtm, time, kubeconform, helm, kubectl)
# were already at their newest release; their findings are Go library
# versions only a publisher's rebuild can move, and the weekly scan says when.

# Base image, on every FROM in lab-image/Dockerfile: the Docker Official
# Image python:3.14.7-slim-trixie, CPython 3.14.7 (python.org, 2026-08-05)
# built on debian:trixie-slim (Debian 13, point release 13.7). The tag
# python:3.14-slim-trixie resolved to the same index digest on 2026-09-25;
# the full tag is written because the tag beside a digest is documentation
# and this one names the patch release.
#
# One base for every stage, the build-only fetch, vendor and mirror stages
# included, rather than debian:trixie-slim for the stages that need no
# Python: the python image IS debian:trixie-slim plus CPython (its linux/amd64
# manifest names debian:trixie-slim's own amd64 digest as its base), so the
# saving would be about 40 MB in stages that never ship, against a second
# digest to keep in step; and vendor-avm.sh then runs at build time on the
# same Python 3.14 the runner ships instead of Debian's python3 (3.13 in
# trixie). No Debian python3 package is installed anywhere in the image.
#
# The FROM lines carry this same reference, because a FROM cannot read a
# file; the publish workflow fails the build if any FROM that is not an
# earlier stage differs from BASE_IMAGE@BASE_DIGEST. The digest is the image
# INDEX digest, from the registry's Docker-Content-Digest header (the method
# vps-agent/lib/capabilities.js documents), cross-checked with
# `docker buildx imagetools inspect`, which reported the same value.
# BASE_PYTHON_VERSION is the CPython release that digest carries; smoke.sh
# compares `python3 --version` with it, so a digest bump that moves Python
# fails until this line moves too. The owner's floor is the newest 3.x line
# at no more than two patch releases behind its latest (3.14.5 while 3.14.7
# is current).
BASE_IMAGE=python:3.14.8-slim-trixie
BASE_DIGEST=sha256:a2b82f3c48559aa0a8446d9af49826b6e2b2016f4cd2afabfe6013ec53729170
BASE_PYTHON_VERSION=3.14.8

# Base of lab-image/sandbox-template/Dockerfile, Docker's Claude Code sandbox
# template (Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS "resolute" on 2026-09-25). Same rule and same
# check as BASE_IMAGE; resolved the same two ways, and unchanged since the
# recipe landed with #676.
SANDBOX_BASE_IMAGE=docker/sandbox-templates:claude-code
SANDBOX_BASE_DIGEST=sha256:868e3f5ef10579e06903d42e86448851ed59319ab8b9fba6dea2772c449bb2a6

# Tools in the runner target.
TERRAFORM_VERSION=1.16.5
TERRAFORM_SHA256=2bc2fcfff033265c9e02ca0351f01794eb122f62a9b2a49a3294b9e49eaab5e4
KUBECONFORM_VERSION=0.8.0
KUBECONFORM_SHA256=9bc2bffbf71f261128533edaf912153948b7ff238f9a531ae6d34466ec287883
HELM_VERSION=4.3.0
HELM_SHA256=86584a54def73570558f66f5111cc53dfed56689637ae32c1201205d494f54fb
# ansible-core, the newest stable line. 2.21's controller range is Python
# 3.12 to 3.14 in the support matrix
# (https://docs.ansible.com/projects/ansible/latest/reference_appendices/release_and_maintenance.html,
# read 2026-09-25), and its wheel declares Requires-Python >=3.12; 2.22 was
# at 2.22.0b1, a beta. lab-host/bootstrap.sh pins the same release.
ANSIBLE_CORE_VERSION=2.21.4
ANSIBLE_CORE_SHA256=ebe74d9c8fadcb41ad2151e031bf1e785e3098aaa015019b4e19a0a96f0dcc4f
# ansible-core's dependencies and theirs, each the newest release inside the
# range its dependant declares, as the one wheel pip selects for CPython 3.14
# on linux x86_64 (cryptography publishes six manylinux x86_64 wheels; this is
# the cp311-abi3-manylinux_2_34 one). One per line in pip's requirements
# syntax. The fetch stage downloads them, and the runner installs them, in
# pip's hash-checking mode: --require-hashes refuses a wheel whose SHA256
# differs, and also refuses to resolve any dependency that is not listed here
# with a hash, so a new transitive dependency fails the build instead of
# arriving unpinned.
ANSIBLE_CORE_DEPS='
jinja2==3.1.6 --hash=sha256:85ece4451f492d0c13c5dd7c13a64681a86afae63a5f347908daf103ce6d2f67
markupsafe==3.0.3 --hash=sha256:457a69a9577064c05a97c41f4e65148652db078a3a509039e64d3467b9e7ef97
pyyaml==6.0.3 --hash=sha256:c458b6d084f9b935061bc36216e8a69a7e293a2f1e68bf956dcd9e6cbcd143f5
cryptography==50.0.1 --hash=sha256:51afcfceb15597cf2635068e4ac9a56b2abde622edde17f37d85fd7b5306497a
cffi==2.1.1 --hash=sha256:b0431303acaea1089ad4b3e9ce4e6518193def1118d4073ca848635ee4ea2e96
pycparser==3.0 --hash=sha256:b727414169a36b7d524c1c3e31839a521725078d7b2ff038656844266160a992
packaging==26.3 --hash=sha256:d7193f7c8e4e93f444fde0262bf90af30e16fa0ad0ad44cb553c87339b23cd1c
resolvelib==1.2.1 --hash=sha256:fb06b66c8da04172d9e72a21d7d06186d8919e32ae5ab5cdf5b9d920be805ac2
'

# Kubernetes JSON schemas for kubeconform, so the `kubeconform` capability
# validates with no network (#675): one directory of
# github.com/yannh/kubernetes-json-schema (the repository kubeconform reads
# over HTTPS by default) at a pinned commit, mirrored to
# /opt/kubeconform/schemas/<dir> under the name kubeconform's own location
# template expects. The commit is content-addressed; the SHA256 is the tree
# hash of the checked-out directory by the same pipeline AVM_CHILD_MODULES
# documents below, so a moved branch and a changed file both fail the build.
# The version matches KUBECTL_VERSION; bump the two together.
KUBERNETES_JSON_SCHEMA_COMMIT=a6f9a32d2ccb64b6e4f5b41419b9c2e8ee0cce18
KUBERNETES_JSON_SCHEMA_DIR=v1.37.1-standalone-strict
KUBERNETES_JSON_SCHEMA_SHA256=fc44a2541c357219c7253e12c2667d20edf088e920123806fe48e5aa6d156fc9

# Tools added by the full target.
KUBECTL_VERSION=1.37.1
KUBECTL_SHA256=65691ff77eb6fa44c908b77a1082c9f092c3b9733b5cefabec0d1104890e21a8
# Azure CLI: the upstream release, installed from Microsoft's apt repository
# as the package `azure-cli=<version>-1~<suite>` that Microsoft's install page
# documents. packages.microsoft.com publishes no trixie suite: on 2026-09-25
# https://packages.microsoft.com/repos/azure-cli/dists/ listed bookworm,
# bullseye, jammy, noble and resolute among others and no trixie, and
# https://learn.microsoft.com/cli/azure/install-azure-cli-linux?pivots=apt
# lists Debian 11 and 12 as tested and says, under "No package for your
# distribution", to use the latest Debian suite, bookworm. So the full target
# installs the bookworm build on trixie (AZURE_CLI_SUITE). That build's
# Depends (libc6 >= 2.35, libssl3 >= 3.0.0, libffi8, zlib1g, libbz2-1.0,
# libuuid1, libgcc-s1) are met by trixie's own packages, and the CLI runs on
# the Python it bundles under /opt/az, not on the image's. The sandbox
# template installs the same release from its base's own suite (resolute).
# The apt signing key is verified by SHA256 before it is trusted; it is the
# key the bookworm and resolute suites are signed with.
AZURE_CLI_VERSION=2.91.0
AZURE_CLI_SUITE=bookworm
MICROSOFT_APT_KEY_SHA256=2fa9c05d591a1582a9aba276272478c262e95ad00acf60eaee1644d93941e3c6

# Terraform providers in the filesystem mirror at /opt/terraform/mirror, each
# with the SHA256 of its linux_amd64 zip as the registry reports it.
# azurerm is mirrored twice: 5.x is current, and the AVM modules vendored
# below still constrain to ~> 4.0 / ~> 4.35. modtm and time are not
# in the issue's list but every vendored module requires them, so without
# them no vendored module could init offline.
PROVIDER_AZURERM_VERSION=5.9.0
PROVIDER_AZURERM_SHA256=44a755607e385f5811e6eb2f73016f9bab73340d138528da73bb0cf994f7524f
PROVIDER_AZURERM_V4_VERSION=4.81.0
PROVIDER_AZURERM_V4_SHA256=79a8d17fefe647040fcb9ee8821a4f09f395427c4fd49493489b9a93a9a1038e
PROVIDER_AZAPI_VERSION=2.13.0
PROVIDER_AZAPI_SHA256=bbe4a39522cff59977e1bf623e7d95267d819ef3cf9ba0f597eb066ce1b11b70
PROVIDER_ALZ_VERSION=0.22.0
PROVIDER_ALZ_SHA256=91e88646e140a728de20c8f66c5fb9e56c240e7c0eab3c1e0f127932c2418fba
PROVIDER_RANDOM_VERSION=3.9.1
PROVIDER_RANDOM_SHA256=60b4f8a8ef18f52bf8e19215229dae408bee732825964092db7c989fd2de4097
PROVIDER_MODTM_VERSION=0.4.0
PROVIDER_MODTM_SHA256=6968bbd28ccdeefa33a77393e1695a896b02e6eeab6ca3384a371675e86587f4
PROVIDER_TIME_VERSION=0.14.2
PROVIDER_TIME_SHA256=0aa1028d91041f4dceba193e3707dac57358d0063d97e20700e554758b67baca

# The builder modules: every Azure Verified Module the Landing Zone Builder
# emits, at the version it emits (ADR 0032 decision 5), vendored at
# /opt/avm/<name>@<version> from the GitHub release source tarball of each
# repository (Azure/terraform-azurerm-<name>, tag v<version>). The SHA256 is
# of the tarball.
#
# One AVM_<KEY>_VERSION / AVM_<KEY>_SHA256 pair per entry of AVM_MODULES in
# frontend/src/lib/landingZone/avmVersions.js, <KEY> being the module name
# upper-cased with `-` as `_`, and nothing else. The Dockerfile's fetch stage
# vendors every pair it finds here, so the list is written once, in this
# block. scripts/lab-image-avm-vendoring.test.mjs fails the `scripts
# (operations)` CI job when this block and avmVersions.js disagree about a
# name or a version in either direction, and update-avm-versions.yml moves a
# pair here in the same pull request that moves the builder's pin. Until
# 2026-09-27 only the three pattern modules were here, and the spokes'
# avm-res-network-virtualnetwork 0.22.2 did not init offline.
#
# avm-ptn-alz-application-landing-zone-identity-and-access, the application
# landing zone pattern module #658 names, is neither emitted nor vendored: on
# 2026-09-25 its repository had no release and no tag, and its main branch
# was still the unmodified AVM template (README title
# "terraform-azurerm-avm-template", a resource named
# azurerm_resource_group.TODO). Add it to avmVersions.js and here together
# when a release exists.
AVM_PTN_ALZ_VERSION=0.21.0
AVM_PTN_ALZ_SHA256=eb2429bfbf4ec5a76b28ffa757ae6ff29e34ea7a84831a9a318809307ca698d8
AVM_PTN_ALZ_MANAGEMENT_VERSION=0.9.0
AVM_PTN_ALZ_MANAGEMENT_SHA256=0536d6050df25ebb53f0f562b8dba5db7264f5323dc333167098a1b743c7281b
AVM_PTN_ALZ_CONNECTIVITY_HUB_AND_SPOKE_VNET_VERSION=0.17.5
AVM_PTN_ALZ_CONNECTIVITY_HUB_AND_SPOKE_VNET_SHA256=dcfa905c0ce4885c29431f644411069dcdfa3d5fc008954a5389815f48239519
# Resolved 2026-09-27: v0.22.2 is the registry's latest release (published
# 2026-08-28), and the sum is of the tarball downloaded that day.
AVM_RES_NETWORK_VIRTUALNETWORK_VERSION=0.22.2
AVM_RES_NETWORK_VIRTUALNETWORK_SHA256=79b07ec98420a0d1013de223e296cbbe130770f0561f71090e1deb9eb561260d

# The registry modules the builder modules call, transitively, vendored
# beside them by vendor-avm.sh (#675), in two blocks the build prints and
# checks together.
#
# AVM_CHILD_MODULES pins each child once, as `<name>@<version> <hash>`. The
# version is what the calling module's constraint resolved to (the registry
# pins each to a commit, so the same constraint resolves the same until the
# caller is bumped). The hash is of the vendored tree after pruning examples,
# tests and every dot-prefixed entry:
#   find . -type f -print0 | LC_ALL=C sort -z | xargs -0 sha256sum | sha256sum
# run inside /opt/avm/<name>@<version>. The build fails on a mismatch, on a
# child it vendored that is missing here, and on a line here nothing calls.
#
# AVM_CHILD_CALLS records which builder module's tree reaches which child:
# one `<builder>@<version> <child>@<version>` line per pair, or the builder
# module alone on its line when it calls no registry module. It is keyed by
# the builder module's VERSION on purpose. A builder pin bump leaves the new
# version with no line here, and scripts/lab-image-avm-vendoring.test.mjs
# fails on exactly that, with no network, because the children a new release
# calls are unknown until the build resolves them; the build fails too, on
# any difference between these lines and what `terraform get` resolved. Two
# versions of one module coexist as two directories: the connectivity module
# reaches avm-res-network-virtualnetwork@0.15.0 while the builder's spokes
# call 0.22.2.
#
# To refresh both after a builder module bump, print them with
#   docker build --target vendor --build-arg AVM_PRINT_PINS=1 --progress=plain lab-image
# and paste the two blocks it prints over these two (README "Updating a
# version" has the one-line form that prints only the blocks).
AVM_CHILD_MODULES='
avm-ptn-network-private-link-private-dns-zones@0.23.2 a04f68ea7afce4a8fd71a41443ae5adbe4c999d6e8de8b1edea5cea92567db15
avm-res-network-azurefirewall@0.4.0 d2d73c553d85227d5cef9f6648c8b08e3d274d1f050a6fcac450cac11c784b20
avm-res-network-bastionhost@0.6.0 52bb44e545947b32e9cf0fc8471751310b5d632c1d9ca3915c7eb10c565353ac
avm-res-network-ddosprotectionplan@0.3.0 2da2f4a4209214ee1fb939fc85e370770f4a0b02955b1c9c544bf14ef13ab95a
avm-res-network-dnsresolver@0.7.3 a9a64e6a87105bca6d26516f49f623435ea2687cbf7252996fafc3fc6b14326c
avm-res-network-firewallpolicy@0.3.3 c4c32031231a8c5e49705b373a2ced7364cb1e937ee787a8fba3bf856c8a91b7
avm-res-network-natgateway@0.3.2 a8431e54bd4112aeb3394e9057776823f68c4f57037bc2787e0177a04de8a81a
avm-res-network-privatednszone@0.4.3 b12674bd3114b0a1554b412496bfa821680302522e053e1a7b63de3a2cc1c669
avm-res-network-publicipaddress@0.2.0 5db447f92a544bbdb1123a8a596debbdf37eb90479462c4087d5f3f6b9ad9fd4
avm-res-network-routetable@0.3.1 23f928962c3e405909c26680cc0080d973c05353c796384f071d1c9c20025e85
avm-res-network-routetable@0.5.0 4dcd9d2404b10b65d444d1b36e57cd921064ce7da3e74471535fea8f47a59396
avm-res-network-virtualnetwork@0.15.0 231d74a31afc362d083160a3f3a891a3e37fc474968ca83b298f5842518ceaae
avm-utl-interfaces@0.2.0 588be3fc801c69861323748fe4bacad65f82b4727a0041709e831995c0726764
avm-utl-interfaces@0.5.0 bcc6a4222313712cf89684e9e325a3116ad6f5801b74b79e08b622ebbc13673b
avm-utl-interfaces@0.6.0 17c3f074415831539520cec5534ce269daf0d7f24c71ea7c5126f28e8d6bb8c5
